From 701c4d1a2dbe5108b2b36dc2285853455224e5c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 07:17:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Phase E: BrowserFragment toolbar/address-bar row -> Compose

Toolbar/address-bar row (home, address pill w/ lock icon + text field +
bookmark star, new-tab, tabs w/ count badge, overflow, progress line) is
now a single ComposeView hosting a new BrowserToolbarRow composable
(BrowserToolbar.kt), replacing 9 findViewById'd Views in fragment_browser.xml
(newTabButton, homeButton, urlInput, tabsButton, tabsCount, overflowButton,
pageProgress, siteSecurityIcon, bookmarkStarButton).

- New BrowserToolbar.kt: BrowserToolbarRow + private AddressPill/
  ToolbarIconButton/TabsButton, Material3, matches AddressBarSuggestions/
  TabsListOverlay conventions.
- fragment_browser.xml: old MaterialCardView + LinearProgressIndicator
  block replaced with a single browserToolbar ComposeView.
- BrowserFragment.kt: 9 lateinit View fields -> 1 ComposeView field + a
  block of mutableStateOf toolbar state fields; every call site that
  touched the old Views updated to read/write the new state
  (onPageStarted/onProgressChanged, updateSecurityIcon, updateBookmarkStar,
  applyTabUiState, loadUrl, showSpeedDial, updateTabsCount,
  AddressBarSuggestions.onTap, ShortcutsScreen.onOpenUrl). setupAddressBar()
  removed -- its editor-action/TextWatcher/focus-change logic now lives in
  BrowserToolbarRow's onGo/onAddressTextChange/onAddressFocusChange
  callbacks, wired once in onViewCreated.
- MainActivity.kt: openBrowserMenu's anchor is now the browserToolbar
  ComposeView itself (a real View) instead of the old overflow ImageButton,
  since the button is no longer a real View to anchor a PopupMenu to.
- Deleted app/src/main/res/drawable/bg_tabs_counter.xml (orphaned --
  reproduced as a Modifier.border in TabsButton).
- COMPOSE_MIGRATION_V2-2.md: Phase E marked DONE with implementation notes
  and deviations from the original plan (direct XML replacement instead of
  a togglable dual-path, once cross-reference grep came back clean).

Cross-reference grep after: zero remaining references anywhere in
app/src/main/java or app/src/main/res to the 9 old view IDs or the deleted
drawable. Not verified against a real build -- no local Android SDK/Gradle
in this environment; flagged for the project's GitHub Actions CI same as
every prior phase.
