 ## Phase E — BrowserFragment chrome, part 1: toolbar + address bar row
 
+**Status: DONE.** The toolbar/address-bar row — home button, the address
+pill (lock icon + text field + bookmark star), new-tab button, tabs
+button w/ live count badge, overflow button — plus the
+`LinearProgressIndicator` that used to sit on the card's bottom edge, are
+now a single `ComposeView` (`browserToolbar` in `fragment_browser.xml`)
+hosting a new `BrowserToolbarRow` composable (`BrowserToolbar.kt`), hosted
+the same way `AddressBarSuggestions` already is — own `ComposeView`,
+anchored in the same position the old `MaterialCardView` + progress line
+occupied. `BrowserViewModel`'s `tabs` list is still a plain
+`mutableListOf` (confirmed by reading it this phase, per Step 4's own
+instruction to check first) — not Flow-backed, so no `StateFlow`
+conversion was needed; the new composable reads plain `by mutableStateOf`
+fields on `BrowserFragment` itself (`addressBarText`, `securityIconVisible`,
+`bookmarkStarVisible`, `toolbarProgress`, `tabsCountValue`, etc.), same
+"field on the Fragment, composable renders it" pattern
+`browserDialogHost`/`suggestionsCard`/`tabsListOverlay` already use
+elsewhere in this file — this is Fragment-local UI state, not repository
+data, so the Bookmark/History/Queue-repository `StateFlow` treatment
+doesn't apply here. Every tap routes back to the exact same functions the
+old View listeners called (`addNewTab()`, `goHome()`, `showTabsOverlay()`,
+`onBookmarkStarTapped()`, `Callbacks.openBrowserMenu()`) — none of that
+destination logic moved, only how it's triggered. One real adaptation:
+`overflowButton.setOnClickListener { openBrowserMenu(overflowButton) }`
+anchored a framework `PopupMenu` to itself; the overflow button is no
+longer a real `View` once it's a Compose `IconButton`, so
+`openBrowserMenu`'s anchor is now the `browserToolbar` `ComposeView`
+itself (still a real `View`, `Gravity.END` still right-aligns the menu
+under it). `EditText`'s built-in `selectAllOnFocus`/`setOnFocusChangeListener`
+select-all-on-focus is reproduced inside the composable's own
+`onFocusChanged` (mutates its local `TextFieldValue` selection directly)
+rather than being reported up to the Fragment — nothing outside the
+composable needs to know the selection range. The old
+`urlInput.clearFocus()` + `hideSoftInputFromWindow()` pair at the end of
+`loadUrl()` couldn't stay an imperative call once focus lives inside a
+child composable, so it's now a one-shot `addressBarClearFocusSignal++`
+the composable's own `LaunchedEffect` reacts to.
+
+Deviation from the original plan below: **the old XML was replaced
+directly**, not left in place togglable behind a visibility flag as
+"Not deletable this phase" originally called for. Cross-reference grep
+after the rewrite found zero remaining references anywhere in
+`app/src/main/java` or `app/src/main/res` to the nine old IDs
+(`newTabButton`, `homeButton`, `urlInput`, `tabsButton`, `tabsCount`,
+`overflowButton`, `pageProgress`, `siteSecurityIcon`,
+`bookmarkStarButton`) — every call site in `BrowserFragment.kt` that used
+to touch one of those Views (`onPageStarted`/`onProgressChanged` in the
+`WebViewClient`/`WebChromeClient`, `updateSecurityIcon`,
+`updateBookmarkStar`, `applyTabUiState`, `loadUrl`, `showSpeedDial`,
+`updateTabsCount`, the `AddressBarSuggestions.onTap` lambda,
+`ShortcutsScreen.onOpenUrl`) was updated in the same pass to read/write
+the new Compose state fields instead, so there was nothing left for a
+toggle to protect — same direct-replacement approach Phase 5's earlier
+`AddressBarSuggestions`/`TabsListOverlay` conversions and this doc's own
+Phase D used once a cross-reference check came back clean, rather than
+carrying a temporary dual-path. `bg_tabs_counter.xml` (the tab-count
+badge's stroke background) is now orphaned — its 1.6dp stroke/6dp corner
+radius is reproduced with a plain Compose `Modifier.border`, so the
+drawable was deleted rather than left unused. Caught and fixed the same
+XML-comment `--` pitfall Phase D's CI run flagged (one new comment in
+`fragment_browser.xml` used it as a dash) before it could repeat that
+failure. **Not verified against a real build** — no local Android
+SDK/Gradle in this environment; verify via the project's GitHub Actions
+CI (`assembleRelease`) same as every prior phase, and pay particular
+attention to `BasicTextField`'s `KeyboardOptions`/`ImeAction.Go` behavior
+and the `LinearProgressIndicator` lambda-`progress` overload (needs
+Material3 1.2+, present via this project's compose-bom 2024.09.00) on a
+real device/emulator, since neither could be exercised here.
+
+Original plan (kept for context):
+
 **Scope:** first real cut into `BrowserFragment.kt`. Do NOT attempt the
 whole file in one phase — 1694 lines, WebView pool, tabs, DNS, sniffer all
 live here. This phase is toolbar + address bar row ONLY.
